             self.extra_delta_transform = True
             self.action_train_with_rotation_6d = False
 
+Prediction and Execution Horizons
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+For ``model_type: openpi``, ``actor.model.openpi.action_horizon`` controls the
+number of future actions loaded and predicted during SFT. The offline SFT loss
+includes every predicted step and only the physical ``action_env_dim`` channels;
+the padded action channels are excluded. ``action_chunk`` controls how many
+predictions inference returns before replanning. For example, predict/train on
+50 steps and execute 20 with these overrides:
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   actor.model.openpi.action_horizon=50 \
+   actor.model.openpi.action_chunk=20 \
+   actor.model.num_action_chunks=20
+
+This corresponds to LeRobot's ``chunk_size=50`` and ``n_action_steps=20``.
+DAgger retains its loss mask over the executed action chunk.
+
 Normalization Statistics
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
@@ -145,6 +164,22 @@ The OpenPI loader later reads the normalization stats from ``<model_path>/<repo_
 
 A practical tip for stable training is to manually check the normalization statistics for very small standard deviations or narrow q99–q01 ranges. Increasing the standard deviation or widening the q99–q01 gap can help stabilize training, especially in two-stage pipelines that transition from SFT to online training.
 
+Initialize from a Previous SFT Checkpoint
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Set ``actor.model.model_path`` to the previous checkpoint directory and keep
+``runner.resume_dir=null`` to load its model weights with a fresh optimizer,
+scheduler, and step counter. This differs from resuming the saved training state.
+
+Checkpoint normalization is checked against any external statistics by default.
+If a new fine-tuning dataset deliberately uses different statistics, explicitly
+add ``+actor.model.allow_norm_stats_override=true`` and set
+``actor.model.openpi_data.norm_stats_path`` to that dataset's statistics.
+The source checkpoint is left intact and future checkpoints bundle the new
+statistics. The initial model's physical input/output mapping changes with the
+normalization, so this option is intended for a new training stage; keep the
+default normalization check for inference and checkpoint resume.
+
 Installation
