        ├── distributed.py                       # sharded-inference helpers
        └── mixture_config.py                    # meta/mixture_config.yaml tag I/O
+
+Local LBench H50/E20 recipe
+----------------------------------------
+
+The ``lbench_steam_value``, ``lbench_steam_advantages``, and ``lbench_cfgrl``
+configs target the local eight-task datasets and two GPUs. Run
+``bash examples/offline_rl/run_lbench_steam.sh check`` for CPU preprocessing
+parity checks, then use the ``value``, ``advantages``, and ``policy`` stages.
+Set ``STEAM_VALUE_CHECKPOINT`` to the trained critic's actor directory before
+labeling. The default critic configuration uses all expert episodes; independent
+episode-level validation must be added before selecting on generalization.
+
+CFG inherits normalization and compatibility metadata from the SFT checkpoint,
+retains FP32 parameters with BF16 AMP, supervises all 50 predicted actions on
+8 physical channels, and executes 20 actions. Guidance tokenization receives
+normalized state before padding, and inference preserves all three cameras.
+Initialization uses model weights with ``runner.resume_dir=null``. The generated
+advantage files must exist before policy training; the recipe does not launch
+simulation evaluation automatically.
